# CareSlot Environment Variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file:  cp .env.example .env.local
#   2. Fill in the real values from your Supabase project dashboard.
#   3. NEVER commit .env.local — it is in .gitignore.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Supabase ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Your project's REST/API URL.
# Found in: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API → Project URL
# ⚠️  DEV PROJECT ONLY — the SQL seed script drops and recreates all tables.
SUPABASE_URL=https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co

# Service-role SECRET key (bypasses Row Level Security).
# Found in: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API → service_role (secret)
# ❌ NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_  — this key must never reach the browser.
# ❌ NEVER log this value anywhere.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...your-service-role-jwt...

# ── Google Gemini ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Gemini API key for the function-calling LLM backend.
# Found in: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# ❌ NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_
GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...your-gemini-api-key...

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHAT NOT TO ADD HERE
#
# ✗  NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY  → would expose secret to browser
# ✗  NEXT_PUBLIC_GEMINI_API_KEY             → would expose secret to browser
#
# If you need a public Supabase key for client-side auth (not used in this
# project), use NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY — but note that all five
# CareSlot tables have RLS enabled with no anon policies, so the anon key
# cannot read or write any data.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
